cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FLAT, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "FLAT: Flattening spectra using the Local Aperiodic Trend"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Haase
    given-names: Tobias C.
    affiliation: University of Tübingen
  - family-names: Gais
    given-names: Steffen
    affiliation: University of Tübingen
abstract: >-
  FLAT separates an EEG or MEG power spectrum into its smooth aperiodic
  background, the baseline, and the periodic activity on top of it. Dividing
  power by the baseline gives a flattened spectrum in which oscillations stand
  out as peaks above 1. Implementations in MATLAB and Python, with examples.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23548995
repository-code: "https://github.com/SteffenGais/FLAT"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - EEG
  - MEG
  - sleep
  - power spectrum
  - aperiodic
  - oscillations
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-21"
